   "stem": {
      "text": "Suppose \\( \\int_{-2}^{-1} f(x)\\,dx = -3 \\) and \\( \\int_{-2}^{1} f(x)\\,dx = -3 \\). The function h is defined by \\( h(x) = -1 \\) for \\( x < 0 \\) and \\( h(x) = 2 \\) for \\( x \\ge 0 \\). Find \\( \\int_{-1}^{1} \\left(2f(x) + h(x)\\right)\\,dx \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 1
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Split the interval at x = -1: \\( \\int_{-1}^{1} f(x)\\,dx = -3 + 3 = 0 \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
         "rule_named": "additivity over adjacent intervals"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "h jumps at x = 0, so split its integral there: \\( -1 \\cdot 1 + 2 \\cdot 1 = 1 \\).",
         "rule_named": "integral of a step function split at the jump"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "By linearity, \\( \\int_{-1}^{1} \\left(2f(x) + h(x)\\right)\\,dx = 2(0) + 1 = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
